    "1990": {"above": ["    ; Foe 18 also runs this tail when it is hit (see foe18_hit): it then puts foe 17, not", "    ; itself, to sleep and jumps into foe 17's loop. Foe 22 wakes foe 17 again in the same tick."]},
    "2021": {"label_above": ["", "; BUG IN THE ORIGINAL DATA, KEPT AS IT IS (bug-for-bug port).", "; Most foes of this sector rise from the bottom (loc_1774) and pop. Each one's hit script starts with", "; \"Loop_Counter0_Back_To <its own hit label> 1\": a hit can come in the middle of the rise,", "; which counts with counter 0, and this loop counts counter 0 down to 0 within the tick, so", "; the restarted rise is a full one.", "; Foe 18's script is a copy of foe 17's, and the copy kept foe 17's label in the loop. So", "; unless counter 0 is exactly 1 at the hit, foe 18 jumps into foe17_hit and runs foe 17's", "; tail: it pops as usual, then puts foe 17 to sleep (foe 22 wakes it again in the same tick)", "; and jumps to loc_1961, so from then on foe 18 runs foe 17's loop: same place, only the", "; picture each rise starts with differs. That Put_Foe_To_Sleep also ends foe 18's interrupt:", "; the original ends the interrupt of the foe running it, whichever foe it names (DESIGN 3.5,", "; opcode 8). In play it looks almost right: foe 18 pops and starts again from the bottom."], "inline": "; original slip: foe17_hit instead of foe18_hit"},
